 "brief_summary": "The purpose of this study is to evaluate the safety and efficacy of a range of doses of SK-0403 in subjects with type 2 diabetes that are not adequately controlled on metformin alone.",
 "eligibility": {
  "criteria": "Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Male and female subjects with type 2 diabetes between 18 and 75 years of age, inclusive\n* Screening HbA1c between 7.0% to 10.0% for metformin stable subjects, 6.5% to 9.0% for subjects on metformin and 1 other antidiabetic agent (excluding thiazolidinediones, insulin, or incretin therapies \\[DPP-4 inhibitors and GLP-1 analogues\\]), or 7.5% to 11.0% for subjects on no antidiabetic medication or, if taking metformin, not on a stable dose of 1500 mg/day or maximum tolerated dose.\n* No antidiabetic medication other than metformin for 3 months prior to randomization.\n* Fasting plasma glucose less than 270 mg/dL (15 mmol/L) at screening.\n* Body mass index between 20 kg/m2 and 45 kg/m2 inclusive at screening.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* History of type 1 diabetes.\n* Received treatment with insulin within 30 days of the screening visit or for more than 1 week within 3 months of the screening visit.\n* Use of 3 or more oral antidiabetic medications at the time of the screening visit.",
  "sex": "ALL",
  "minimum_age": "18 Years",
  "maximum_age": "75 Years",
  "healthy_volunteers": false,
  "std_ages": [
   "ADULT",
   "OLDER_ADULT"
  ]
 },
